{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I charged your judges.</b> I urged them to be deliberate: for even though this law had already come before them many times, they should not take it lightly to rush and decide it abruptly, but should engage in thorough give-and-take over the matter." "<b>Hear the cause between your brethren and judge righteously.</b> This is compromise (פשרה), which is the judgment that comes from righteousness (צדק)." "<b>And between his stranger.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even concerning matters of dwelling, such as the division of inheritance among brothers — even between an oven and a stove."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:38.734641753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}